[agent] ## Result
[agent] Feature group **`scaledd69ec7`** version 1 is registered on the platform with:
[agent] - **Record key**: `row_id`
[agent] - **Columns**: `row_id, split, f1, f2, f3, f4`
[agent] - **`online_enabled: true`** — features available for low-latency online/real-time lookup (the platform distinguishes offline vs. online; both were written)
[agent] - **650 rows** — 400 `train` + 250 `serve`
[agent] ## Approach (all compute on-platform)
[agent] 1. Ingested the two CSVs as-is into raw feature groups `scaled_raw_train` / `scaled_raw_serve` via `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. Trino (`hops sql`) could not read these offline tables — the Hopsworks offline format is rejected by both the `hudi` and `iceberg` connectors exposed here ("Not a Hudi/Iceberg table"), and no `hive` catalog is available. So I pivoted to the platform's job runner.
[agent] 3. Wrote a PySpark job and ran it server-side via `hops job deploy ... --type pyspark --run --wait`. The job:
[agent]    - Computed **train-only** mean and **population** standard deviation (`stddev_pop`, no Bessel correction) for f1–f4.
[agent]    - Applied `(x − mean) / std` to **both** splits using those train statistics, `round(..., 6)`.
[agent]    - Labelled rows `train`/`serve` and wrote them to a new online-enabled feature group `scaledd69ec7` v1.
